hdl/ieee1722/avtp/KL_avtp_rx_monitor_ctx.sv:KL_avtp_rx_monitor_ctx: pres_ofs_i — documented in ns, not named for it: presentation offset ns
hdl/ieee1722/avtp/KL_avtp_rx_monitor_ctx.sv:KL_avtp_rx_monitor_ctx: dirty_p_o — documented in second, not named for it: per-context counter-change pulses (Milan 5.4.5 Table 5.22): bit s = context s committed an EVENT its GET_COUNTERS push law cares about. FRAMES_RX alone stays excluded (task #21: a healthy stream closes an interval every second forever), and so does a healthy TV tally (gh #60 F4 option (c) - see the M_PDEC_S site). Was the stream-0 scalar; sinks 1..N-1 could never arm their own Table 5.22 push (gh #60 F2).
hdl/ieee1722/avtp/avtp_stream_parser.sv:avtp_stream_parser: fsh2_o — documented in bytes, not named for it: bytes o+24..31 (CRF ts low)
